    "n1": {
      "x": -940,
      "y": 1400,
      "w": 860,
      "text": "Halyard is a fictional edge deploy platform, drawn end to end so every hard thing a website has to do turns up at least once.\n\nEvery board carries the Fluant Ink tokens as CSS custom properties and reproduces the system's class contract: .fl-btn[data-variant], .fl-table td[data-numeric], .fl-switch[aria-checked]. State lives in ARIA and data-* attributes, never in a class name, so the accessible state and the visual state cannot drift apart.\n\nThat is what makes it portable: emit the same element with the same attributes and the CSS carries the design."
    },
    "n2": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": 10700,
      "w": 390,
      "text": "The phone board is a real 390x844 frame with a working tab bar and a sheet. No painted status bar and no fake keyboard — on a device the real ones render on top."
    }
  },
